course: dictionary
lesson: 6733
title: One word, many meanings: old
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: The word old can mean different things, and the words around it show you which meaning is right. «Tom is 7 years old» tells you how many years Tom has lived.
explain: «Never go into old mines, caves or tunnels; they can collapse or be full of bad air.» Here old means from long ago and no longer used. It does not mean that the mines are older people.
explain: «My old school» means the school you went to before, not one that is old and falling down. «Old mate» is a friendly way to talk to someone, and it does not mean age at all. Always check the clues around the word.
fact: Old can tell how many years someone or something has lived: «Tom is 7 years old».
fact: Old can mean having lived a long time, or from long ago: «an old man», «old diving bells».
fact: Old can mean not new, or used for a long time: «old shoes».
fact: Old can mean from before, as in «my old school». Friendly words like «old mate» are casual, not about age.
fact: Polite words for older people include «elderly», «senior» and «older people».
exercise: «Older children in big families often help a lot, but they still need breakfast, sleep and time for themselves.» In this sentence, what does older mean? | Very angry | Bigger than the others | Left over from yesterday | *More years old than the others
exercise: «Never go into old mines, caves or tunnels.» What does old mean here? | Brand new | Fast-moving | *From long ago and no longer used | Very quiet
exercise: «Tom is 7 years old.» What does years old tell you? | Where Tom lives | What Tom likes to eat | *How many years Tom has lived | How tall Tom is
test: «My old school» means | *A school you went to in the past | A school that is brand new | A school with a big garden | The school with the best food
test: Which word is the form of old that means the most years? | *Oldest | Older | Newest | Oldish
exam: Which of these is a polite word for older people? | Tiny | Loud | Naughty | *Senior
